WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:56.930
<b>Pearl</b>

38
00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.930
All right!

39
00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.770
They wanna fight, too, huh?!

40
00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.810
Now this'll be fun!

41
00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:04.600
Okay, Pops! You promised me, remember?

42
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.820
If I run those pirates off,
then my debt to you is cleared.

43
00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:08.780
No more chores.

44
00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:09.860
That's the deal...

45
00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:12.530
There's no telling how
much more of my restaurant

46
00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.740
you could screw up if you stick around.

47
00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.740
Yeah!

48
00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:20.040
So, kid, you said you were going
to be King of the Pirates...

49
00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.540
Were you serious?

50
00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:26.830
If we can capture that ship, the Grand
Line will be ours for the taking!

51
00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.920
No more pretending to be Marines...

52
00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.840
Or raising the white flag of surrender.

53
00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:37.140
None of our enemies will suspect that
we're a threat with a ship like that.

54
00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.560
In that boat, it'll
always be a sneak attack.

55
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.850
He's right. That boat
would come in handy.

56
00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:47.020
No one would think that pirates were
on such a ridiculous-looking ship.

57
00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.440
Right, but Don...

58
00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:51.690
Even if we enter the Grand Line
again using that vessel...

59
00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.990
What if we come across someone
like Hawk-Eye Mihawk again?!

60
00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:56.320
Then what'll we do?

61
00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:03.160
I really appreciate the input,
Sailor, anything else? Huh?!

62
00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.040
N... No!

63
00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.000
Do you think an ordinary man could
cut up a sailing ship like that?!

64
00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.970
That man probably has
the power of the devil fruit.

65
00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:18.010
Although those with devil fruit
powers are rare and legendary to us...

66
00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:21.890
I assure you they're
commonplace on the Grand Line.

67
00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:26.940
Mihawk must've used some sort of strange
power when he sliced our ship to ribbons.

68
00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.610
When we're on the Grand Line,
those powers won't be special.

69
00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.530
Even the straw hat freak
will be considered normal.

70
00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:40.370
That old geezer, Red Foot Zeff,
sailed those seas for a year.

71
00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.370
It stands to reason that he had
strategies for dealing with those monsters.

72
00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.340
The techniques for surviving
that parade of weirdos

73
00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:57.470
must be written in the old man's logbook...
along with clues to the One Piece.

74
00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.840
I see... You're a genius!

75
00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.470
All we have to do is get
that logbook and the ship,

76
00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.310
then we'll be able to find our
way to the One Piece again!

77
00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.810
Ya hear that, boys?!

78
00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:09.650
Now let's get to it!
That restaurant will be ours!

79
00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:15.150
You pirate scum are gonna
hafta get through us first!

80
00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.780
Go to the control room,
and open up the fins.

81
00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:21.120
What?! No! That's a bad idea!

82
00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.660
If we do that, we'll be
giving the enemy a foothold!

83
00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.200
And that's just fine.
We gotta do whatever it takes

84
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.500
to keep those guys out of this place.

85
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.250
If they destroy the inside, then
the old man'll complain forever.

86
00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.380
Did you just say something, you brat?

87
00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.590
Yeah... I said you're whiney!

88
00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:37.130
Now go.

89
00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.470
Yes, sir!

90
00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.550
That's right... Bring it on!

91
00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.770
I'm comin' for ya!

92
00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.020
Gum-Gum... Rocket!

93
00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.770
He's flying over this way!

94
00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.770
And Gum-Gum...

95
00:04:53.770 --> 00:05:00.150
... Giant Scythe!

96
00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:09.540
Didja see that?! Go, Kid!

97
00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.460
What the heck's
up with that guy?!

98
00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.710
Yeah! He's crazy!

99
00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:14.290
It's hard to believe...

100
00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.340
The Grand Line is crawling
with guys like these?

101
00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.630
Sanji...

102
00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.050
Pay special attention
to how this one fights.

103
00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:23.680
So Let me get this straight...

104
00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:26.180
You're attacking the
restaurant that gave you food?

105
00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:29.020
I got no choice but to beat
some manners into you!

106
00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:34.810
So you wanna fight on the water
where there's no place to stand, huh?

107
00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.980
A bold move for someone like you.

108
00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:41.530
The devil fruit has taken your ability
to swim, hasn't it... Chore Boy!

109
00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.870
Yeah, but now... I'm stretchy!

110
00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:49.250
Sanji... Here come the fins!

111
00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:03.800
What is this?!

112
00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.640
Now we have
somewhere to fight 'em!

113
00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.900
Whoa! That's so cool!

114
00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.620
My cooks and I will never give
up defending this place...

115
00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.620
Prepare to die.

116
00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:30.870
I see...

117
00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.830
Good plan, bringing up all
that extra decking, genius.

118
00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.630
Now we don't have to
take the fight inside.

119
00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.960
I'd hate to damage my future ship...

120
00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.220
And make no mistake, it will be mine!

121
00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:46.050
We will never let
you have the restaurant!

122
00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.350
That's right! We mean business!

123
00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:49.850
We're battle cooks now!

124
00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:02.860
Set sail, Mackerel Head One,
the Baratie's secret weapon!

125
00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:06.700
So If you wanna live,
I'd suggest running away now!

126
00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.740
What is that thing?

127
00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:14.210
That thing is so... cool!

128
00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:15.580
Paddle faster!

129
00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:16.920
You paddle faster!

130
00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:20.000
Fire!

131
00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:26.930
Those guys
are gonna sink me, too!

132
00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:28.680
Yeah! Get 'em!

133
00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.140
Yeah!

134
00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:33.520
Get 'em, guys! Get 'em!
Blow 'em away! You can do it!

135
00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:37.060
Nice!

136
00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.900
Keep your eyes on the prize, Patty!

137
00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:42.400
This one counts!

138
00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:46.780
Right! Krieg! Say your prayers!

139
00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:49.620
Little did you know that
the Sea Restaurant Baratie

140
00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.910
had such a powerful weapon
just waiting to be unleashed!

141
00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.590
What happened?!
Did we bump into something?

142
00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:05.840
We're not moving!

143
00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:09.180
I am Don Krieg...

144
00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:12.470
... the man who will rule... the oceans!

145
00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:14.430
Oh no, you're not... I am!

146
00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.600
I don't have time for
these stupid games!

147
00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.890
Get outta here!

148
00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.400
No way! He's so strong!

149
00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:35.040
It's coming straight for us!

150
00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:38.080
The restaurant...! Oh no!

151
00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:56.470
Sanji!

152
00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.270
No way!

153
00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.570
He's got legs of steel!

154
00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:15.950
He kicked back that crazy boat
just like it was nothing!

155
00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.750
Very impressive.

156
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.040
Nice kick!

157
00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.750
What's the deal?!

158
00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.800
Are you trying to crush your friends?!

159
00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:27.710
Yeah, yeah.

160
00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.630
Don't "yeah, yeah" us, you crazy fool!

161
00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.130
Stop acting so cool!

162
00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.550
You wouldn't be so smug if we'd
been killed, you bucket of backwash!

163
00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:39.600
All right, ladies, you think
you could wrap this up another time?

164
00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.480
We have business to attend to.

165
00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:42.730
Get them!

166
00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:52.360
You guys still don't get it.

167
00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:55.030
Even well armed,
you're still just cooks,

168
00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:57.410
and we're expert fighters that
are way out of your league.

169
00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:01.160
So why don't you be good little cooks,
and run along to a safer restaurant?

170
00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.370
Maybe one on land, huh?

171
00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:06.040
C'mon, guys, why are you lettin'
'em beat you up so easily, huh?

172
00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:09.130
And you still call
yourselves fighting cooks?!

173
00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.920
Well, these pirates are really good!

174
00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.380
They're totally different from
the ones we've fought before!

175
00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:16.970
It's insulting to lump us in
with that average riffraff...

176
00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.600
We are the great Krieg Pirates!

177
00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:21.230
And we're the absolute
rulers of the East Blue!

178
00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:25.150
Let it be known to all... that
this garish boat already belongs...

179
00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:27.310
... to the great and
powerful Krieg Pirates!

180
00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.900
You know what,
I've been a cook all my life!

181
00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.240
I've worked at a lot of restaurants,

182
00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.910
and gotten fired from them all
for scuffling and livin' hard!

183
00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:38.910
And after years of wandering,
we finally found a home here!

184
00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.910
Anybody here!

185
00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:48.380
<b>Help
 Wanted</b>

186
00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:45.540
This is the restaurant that's owned
by a guy name Red Foot Zeff, right?!

187
00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:48.380
Hey! We found this "Damn Cooks
Wanted" sign, is it true?!

188
00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:53.260
Yeah... It's true.

189
00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:59.720
But you need to understand that
this is no ordinary restaurant.

190
00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:03.180
It really doesn't matter who they
are... or where they come from...

191
00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:07.650
... if someone comes in hungry...
we will feed them until they're stuffed!

192
00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:11.440
Do I make myself clear?!
Can you handle that?

193
00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.030
Sir!

194
00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:11.900
<b>Help
 Wanted</b>

195
00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.740
I wouldn't serve anyone slop like this!

196
00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.750
Hey! What'd you go
and hit me for, huh?!

197
00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.710
Share victory! Share defeat!

198
00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:30.250
We like fighting and cooking,
so this place is perfect for us.

199
00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.800
That's right! There's
no other place like this!

200
00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:37.180
You hear that? Now that's
true fighting spirit!

201
00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:40.100
Committing ourselves
to cooking fine cuisine

202
00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.640
day in and day out
is a fierce battle...

203
00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:46.140
Compared to that,
these pirates are nothing!

204
00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.600
He's right. Yeah.

205
00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:48.650
Let's fight!

206
00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:50.480
– Yeah!
– Protect Zeff!

207
00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.610
Protect the restaurant!

208
00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:05.750
Huh? The hell was that?!

209
00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.290
Huh?

210
00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.550
Just what do you
guys think you're doing?

211
00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.890
Who's that? Huh.

212
00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:24.060
So... let's do this...

213
00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:27.850
<b>Pearl "the Invincible"
Second Unit Commander
Krieg Pirates</b>

214
00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:25.770
But... before we begin...

215
00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.850
It's only fair I give you a warning.

216
00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.480
I am Pearl, the Invincible Shield.

217
00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:32.190
Hey, it's Pearl!

218
00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:35.150
Patty! Carne! Are you boys okay?

219
00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.360
I'd say that pair is far from okay.

220
00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.450
Those two just experienced
my Pearl Surprise,

221
00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:42.280
one of my signature punches,
you bumbling, pathetic idiot!

222
00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.450
Hey! Look at that...

223
00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.620
Nice knife... I think I'll take it.

224
00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:52.380
Wha? Give it here... C'mon, let it go!

225
00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:54.000
I said, give it to me!

226
00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:54.800
Huh?

227
00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:09.100
That guy knows how to
kick some serious butt.

228
00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.060
A kitchen knife is a cook's soul!

229
00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:15.690
How dare you filthy pirates try to desecrate
one with your grubby little hands!

230
00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.360
Sanji...

231
00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.240
Just stay down and hang on to this.

232
00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:22.360
I'm gonna teach these bozos a lesson.

233
00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.870
You must be out of your mind

234
00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.200
if you think we're gonna
be beaten by a mere cook!

235
00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:38.010
I'll show you "mere cook" after
I fillet every one of you bastards.

236
00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:42.760
Hah! How very impudent of you
to defeat them all using only your kicks.

237
00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:45.100
Am I to be impressed by that?

238
00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:47.100
I'm a cook, remember?

239
00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:50.520
I couldn't do my job very well
if I ruined my hands in battle.

240
00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:53.060
So I'll be taking you
down with my feet.

241
00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:55.610
Is that so? I think not.

242
00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:57.270
I'm invincible, you see.

243
00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:01.610
I've won all sixty-one of my battles
completely and totally unscathed.

244
00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:02.780
It's quite remarkable, really.

245
00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:06.450
No one has ever shed a single
drop of my blood in battle.

246
00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:07.450
No one.

247
00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.950
Now do you realize my power?!

248
00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.420
I may be a gentleman,
but I'm not gentle...

249
00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:17.840
Got it?

250
00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:19.670
Was that supposed to be a joke?

251
00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.470
'Cause it wasn't even
a little bit funny.

252
00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:25.260
Dropping your guard is a good
way to end up dead, you brat!

253
00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:34.810
Even battleship
cannons don't work on me.

254
00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.400
I come out of any attack unharmed!

255
00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.280
Boy, that could've been really bad.

256
00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.570
Good thing I didn't
fall into the ocean...

257
00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:49.280
